Third-party code
----------------

The ARChitects (Daniel Franzen and Jan Disselhoff)
  ARC Prize 2024 submission code, https://github.com/da-fr/arc-prize-2024,
  Apache License 2.0. NVARC's notebook, and through it ours, builds on this code:
  the data loader and augmentations (ArcDataset), depth-first search decoding and
  candidate selection. Their NOTICE file reads:

    Kaggle ARC Prize 2024 Submission Code
    Copyright 2024 Daniel Franzen and Jan Disselhoff

NVARC (Ivan Sorokin and Jean-François Puget)
  Kaggle notebook sorokin/arc2-qwen3-unsloth-flash-lora-batch4-queue (version 10),
  released on Kaggle under the Apache License 2.0. Our notebooks run its per-task
  test-time training, four-GPU worker queue, kgmon scorer and Qwen formatter.
  Nothing is copied from NVARC's GitHub repository (github.com/1ytic/NVARC), which
  carries no licence.

kaiserm
  Kaggle notebook kaiserm/nvarc-winning-solution-2025-4xl4s (version 2), the public
  2026 port of NVARC's notebook, with seven data-path lines changed. Our notebooks
  are forks of it.


Models, data and packages used but not included
-----------------------------------------------

sorokin/qwen3_4b_grids15_sft139 (Kaggle Models, Apache 2.0)
  NVARC's checkpoint, trained from Qwen3-4B (Qwen team, Apache 2.0). Every
  notebook loads it.

sorokin/pip-install-unsloth-flash-patch (Kaggle notebook by NVARC)
  Attached to every notebook as an input that supplies its Python packages.
  None of its code is copied here.

ARC-GEN (Michael D. Moffitt, https://github.com/google/ARC-GEN, Apache 2.0;
arXiv:2511.00162)
  kaggle_kernel/arc_agi2_sft_syn trains on tasks sampled from the ARC-GEN-100K
  dataset (Kaggle dataset arcgen100k/the-arc-gen-100k-dataset, Apache 2.0).

ARC-AGI-2 tasks
  Kaggle competition arc-prize-2026-arc-agi-2; the public tasks are also at
  https://github.com/arcprize/arc-agi-2 (Apache 2.0). Not redistributed here.
